            <ArticleTitle>The radiographic evolution of a Schmorl's node.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>224-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We present a case showing the development of a Schmorl's node from its acute to chronic stage by serial MRI. In contrast to the mature Schmorl's node, imaging characteristics of the acute Schmorl's node have not been well-illustrated, particularly by contrast-enhanced images at various stages of development.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
